# agent2kb scheduled tasks — template (for supercronic or a regular crontab)
#
# Copy this file to `scripts/kb-crontab` (gitignored) and customise the
# project paths and profile names for your setup. The example uses two
# fictitious projects, `alpha` and `beta`, each with its own .kb/config.yaml.
#
# The Docker image uses docker/crontab.example: the same jobs with container
# paths. Keep the two in step.
#
# Run supercronic with:
#   supercronic /path/to/agent2kb/scripts/kb-crontab
#
# Reload after editing without restarting:
#   kill -USR2 $(pgrep supercronic)
#
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Compile: every 15 minutes. When nothing has changed, the fast path returns in
# about two seconds without using any tokens; the LLM is used only when new raw
# files exist.
*/15 * * * * /path/to/agent2kb/scripts/kb-cron-compile.sh /path/to/alpha alpha
*/15 * * * * /path/to/agent2kb/scripts/kb-cron-compile.sh /path/to/beta  beta

# Lint: daily at 09:00. Structural checks only (no tokens are used).
0 9 * * * /path/to/agent2kb/scripts/kb-cron-lint.sh /path/to/alpha alpha
0 9 * * * /path/to/agent2kb/scripts/kb-cron-lint.sh /path/to/beta  beta

# Backup: twice daily at 02:30 and 14:30. Archives to
# <project>/.backups/<kb>-wiki-YYYY-MM-DD-HHMMSS-<random>.tar.gz (UTC; local, independent
# of S3). Keeps the last 30 archives (about 15 days at two per day). Restore via
# `a2kb restore --date ...`.
30 2,14 * * * /path/to/agent2kb/scripts/kb-cron-backup.sh /path/to/alpha alpha
30 2,14 * * * /path/to/agent2kb/scripts/kb-cron-backup.sh /path/to/beta  beta

# Stubs: daily at 03:00 (after the 02:30 backup, before 09:00 lint).
# Materialises ghost wikilinks (five or more mentions) as placeholder concept
# pages, so that Obsidian readers do not reach "Create new page" prompts.
# Idempotent: existing stubs are refreshed and real pages are never overwritten.
0 3 * * * /path/to/agent2kb/scripts/kb-cron-stubs.sh /path/to/alpha alpha
0 3 * * * /path/to/agent2kb/scripts/kb-cron-stubs.sh /path/to/beta  beta

# Weekly digest: Sundays at 04:00 UTC. Scans the last seven days of
# raw/wiki/concepts/outputs, asks the LLM CLI (codex; configurable with the
# CODEX_BIN environment variable) for an insight digest of 500 to 1500 words,
# then `a2kb promote` saves it to outputs/weekly/<YYYY>-W<NN>.md as a digest
# entry. A run uses roughly 5,000 to 15,000 tokens and happens once a week, so
# the cost is negligible. Stagger the runs across projects to avoid concurrent
# load on codex and S3.
0  4 * * 0 /path/to/agent2kb/scripts/kb-cron-digest.sh /path/to/alpha alpha
30 4 * * 0 /path/to/agent2kb/scripts/kb-cron-digest.sh /path/to/beta  beta
